2026-11-16 13:30:52 | RESPONSE | sactor.llm:160 | The only compile error was that `libc::getc` does not exist in the `libc` crate. I replaced it with `libc::fgetc`, which behaves the same here.

In C, `char ch = getc(fp)` truncates the value to `char`. On x86 `char` is signed, so EOF stays -1. I kept the original `as i8 as i32` cast to preserve that behavior. The rest of the translation is unchanged.

